        <oboInOwl:id>GO:0001846</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that an opsonin is a blood serum protein or fragment which when deposited on the surface of a bacteria, virus, immune complex, or other particulate material acts a signal for phagocytosis to cells bearing the appropriate receptors. Not all complement components or fragments and not all antibodies have opsonic properties.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>opsonin binding</rdfs:label>
