                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0044320"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The series of molecular signals initiated by leptin binding to its receptor on the surface of a cell, and ending with the regulation of a downstream cellular process, e.g. transcription. Leptin is a hormone manufactured primarily in the adipocytes of white adipose tissue, and the level of circulating leptin is directly proportional to the total amount of fat in the body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
